\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Monthly wildfire detection frequency across India (2018--2025, NASA FIRMS VIIRS S-NPP Collection 2). March is the peak fire month with 698k detections, driven by the pre-monsoon dry season. The monsoon period (June--September) nearly eliminates fire activity. A secondary peak occurs in October--November due to agricultural burning and post-monsoon drying. This bimodal seasonality motivates the use of cyclical month encoding and date-conditional negative sampling to prevent the model from exploiting trivial seasonal shortcuts.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:seasonal_freq}{{1}{5}{Monthly wildfire detection frequency across India (2018--2025, NASA FIRMS VIIRS S-NPP Collection 2). March is the peak fire month with 698k detections, driven by the pre-monsoon dry season. The monsoon period (June--September) nearly eliminates fire activity. A secondary peak occurs in October--November due to agricultural burning and post-monsoon drying. This bimodal seasonality motivates the use of cyclical month encoding and date-conditional negative sampling to prevent the model from exploiting trivial seasonal shortcuts}{figure.1}{}}
